Certainly! Merging Word documents with OpenXML SDK is a non-trivial task, especially when you need to:

- Take only the **first 2 pages** from the first document (including **header, footer, styles, and design**).
- Take **only page contents and glossary** from the second document.
- Preserve **images** from both documents.

Below is a high-level solution. Please note that OpenXML doesn't provide a direct “import page” or "merge documents" API. Pages in Word are not explicit elements in the XML, so you need to approximate "pages" by counting paragraphs, sections, and using page breaks.

**Main Steps:**

1. **Extract first 2 pages** from Document 1.
2. **Extract header, footer, and styles** from Document 1.
3. **Extract main content (body) and glossary** from Document 2.
4. **Merge everything** into a new document.

Below is a complete example using OpenXML SDK (`DocumentFormat.OpenXml` NuGet package):

---

### Helper Functions

- You will need helper methods to:
    - Extract N pages from a document.
    - Copy headers, footers, and styles.
    - Append body and glossary content.
    - Copy referenced images/parts.

---

### Sample Implementation

```csharp
using DocumentFormat.OpenXml.Packaging;
using DocumentFormat.OpenXml.Wordprocessing;
using System.IO;
using System.Linq;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class WordMerger
{
    public void MergeDocs(string doc1Path, string doc2Path, string outputPath)
    {
        // 1. Copy doc1 as the base for the output
        File.Copy(doc1Path, outputPath, true);

        using (WordprocessingDocument outDoc = WordprocessingDocument.Open(outputPath, true))
        using (WordprocessingDocument doc1 = WordprocessingDocument.Open(doc1Path, false))
        using (WordprocessingDocument doc2 = WordprocessingDocument.Open(doc2Path, false))
        {
            // 2. Extract and keep only the first 2 pages from doc1's main body in outDoc
            KeepFirstNPages(outDoc, 2);

            // 3. Copy styles from doc1 (already present since we copied doc1 as base)

            // 4. Copy content and glossary from doc2
            AppendBodyContentFromDoc2(outDoc, doc2);
            AppendGlossaryFromDoc2(outDoc, doc2);

            // 5. Copy all referenced images from doc2 to outDoc (for appended content)
            CopyImages(outDoc, doc2);
        }
    }

    // --- Helper: Keep only first N pages (approximate by counting section/page breaks) ---
    private void KeepFirstNPages(WordprocessingDocument doc, int nPages)
    {
        var body = doc.MainDocumentPart.Document.Body;
        var elements = body.Elements().ToList();

        List<OpenXmlElement> keepElements = new List<OpenXmlElement>();
        int pageBreakCount = 0;
        foreach (var elem in elements)
        {
            keepElements.Add(elem.CloneNode(true));
            // Check for explicit page breaks or section breaks
            if (elem is Paragraph para)
            {
                if (para.Descendants<Break>().Any(b => b.Type?.Value == BreakValues.Page))
                    pageBreakCount++;
            }
            if (elem is Paragraph || elem is SectionProperties)
            {
                // SectionProperties typically indicate a section (often a new page)
                if (elem is Paragraph p && p.Descendants<SectionProperties>().Any())
                {
                    pageBreakCount++;
                }
            }
            if (pageBreakCount >= nPages)
                break;
        }

        // Replace body content
        body.RemoveAllChildren();
        foreach (var elem in keepElements)
            body.Append(elem.CloneNode(true));
    }

    // --- Helper: Append body content from doc2 (excluding headers/footers/styles) ---
    private void AppendBodyContentFromDoc2(WordprocessingDocument outDoc, WordprocessingDocument doc2)
    {
        var outBody = outDoc.MainDocumentPart.Document.Body;
        var doc2Body = doc2.MainDocumentPart.Document.Body;

        // Import all elements (deep clone)
        foreach (var elem in doc2Body.Elements())
        {
            outBody.Append(elem.CloneNode(true));
        }
    }

    // --- Helper: Copy glossary (DocumentSettingsPart/GlossaryDocumentPart) ---
    private void AppendGlossaryFromDoc2(WordprocessingDocument outDoc, WordprocessingDocument doc2)
    {
        var glossary = doc2.MainDocumentPart.GlossaryDocumentPart;
        if (glossary != null)
        {
            // Remove existing glossary if present
            var existingGlossary = outDoc.MainDocumentPart.GlossaryDocumentPart;
            if (existingGlossary != null)
            {
                outDoc.MainDocumentPart.DeletePart(existingGlossary);
            }
            // Add glossary part from doc2
            var newGlossary = outDoc.MainDocumentPart.AddNewPart<GlossaryDocumentPart>();
            newGlossary.FeedData(glossary.GetStream());
        }
    }

    // --- Helper: Copy images from doc2 to outDoc, avoiding duplicate ids ---
    private void CopyImages(WordprocessingDocument outDoc, WordprocessingDocument doc2)
    {
        var outMain = outDoc.MainDocumentPart;
        var doc2Main = doc2.MainDocumentPart;

        foreach (var imgPart in doc2Main.ImageParts)
        {
            // Copy image part
            var relId = doc2Main.GetIdOfPart(imgPart);
            if (!outMain.ImageParts.Any(ip => outMain.GetIdOfPart(ip) == relId))
            {
                var newImgPart = outMain.AddImagePart(imgPart.ContentType);
                using (var stream = imgPart.GetStream())
                {
                    newImgPart.FeedData(stream);
                }
                // Remap relId in the document's XML if necessary (advanced: requires rel-id remapping in XML)
            }
        }
    }
}
```

---

### Usage

```csharp
var merger = new WordMerger();
merger.MergeDocs("doc1.docx", "doc2.docx", "merged.docx");
```

---

### Notes

- **Page Extraction:** OpenXML doesn't know about "pages" as layout is handled by Word itself. The code approximates by counting `Break` elements (type Page) and section breaks, but complex layouts may require more sophisticated logic or use of 3rd party libraries.
- **Headers/Footers/Styles:** Since we start by copying doc1, those are preserved.
- **Images:** This code copies image parts, but if the same image is referenced more than once, you'll need to remap rel-ids in your appended content.
- **Glossary:** Copies the entire glossary from doc2, replacing any in doc1.

---

### Limitations

- Rel-ID remapping for images/shapes is a complex task not fully covered here.
- "2 page" extraction is only a rough approximation.
- Complex documents (tables, custom xml, footnotes, etc.) may need more advanced handling.

---

**For production use and more robust merging, consider using commercial libraries (like [Aspose.Words](https://products.aspose.com/words/net/)), as OpenXML SDK is low-level and not optimized for merging.**

