### More Advanced: Cleaned Extraction

If you want to **exclude** text from scripts, styles, and hidden elements, you can further refine it:

```javascript
function extractVisibleText() {
    function getText(node) {
        if (
            node.nodeType === Node.TEXT_NODE &&
            node.parentNode &&
            getComputedStyle(node.parentNode).display !== "none" &&
            getComputedStyle(node.parentNode).visibility !== "hidden"
        ) {
            return node.textContent.trim();
        }
        if (
            node.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE &&
            !['SCRIPT', 'STYLE', 'NOSCRIPT'].includes(node.tagName)
        ) {
            let text = '';
            for (let child of node.childNodes) {
                text += getText(child) + ' ';
            }
            return text;
        }
        return '';
    }
    return getText(document.body).replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
}
```

**Usage:**
```javascript
let visibleText = extractVisibleText();
console.log(visibleText);
```

---

**Summary:**  
- Use `document.body.textContent` for a simple solution.
- Use the advanced function above to filter out hidden/script/style text.

