Here is a Tailscale ACL (`acl:`) configuration that implements your requirements for the three groups: `nill`, `family`, and `servers`.

**Assumptions:**
- You will substitute example emails/IDs with your actual user or device identifiers.
- You will substitute example tags/hostnames with your actual ones.
- All "servers" (regardless of group) are tagged as `tag:server`. Adjust as needed.

```json
{
  "groups": {
    "group:nill": [
      "alice@example.com",
      // Add more users or devices here
    ],
    "group:family": [
      "bob@example.com",
      // Add more users or devices here
    ],
    "group:servers": [
      "carol@example.com",
      // Add more users or devices here
    ]
  },
  "acls": [
    // nill group: access to everything, everywhere
    {
      "action": "accept",
      "users": ["group:nill"],
      "ports": ["*:*"]
    },
    // servers group: access to 22, 80, 443 (tcp only) on all servers
    {
      "action": "accept",
      "users": ["group:servers"],
      "ports": [
        "tag:server:22",
        "tag:server:80",
        "tag:server:443"
      ]
    },
    // family group: NO access to any services (deny everything explicitly)
    {
      "action": "deny",
      "users": ["group:family"],
      "ports": ["*:*"]
    }
  ],
  "tagOwners": {
    "tag:server": ["group:servers", "group:nill"]
    // Add more tag owners if you use tags for subgroups
  },
  // Allow family to use any node as an exit node (but not access services)
  "exitNodeACLs": [
    {
      "users": ["group:family"],
      "exitNodeIps": ["*"]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Explanation

- **nill**: `*:*` means full access to all services on all nodes. This group can do everything.
- **servers**: Access to **only** ports 22/tcp, 80/tcp, 443/tcp on any server tagged as `tag:server`. No other ports/protocols.
- **family**: Explicit `deny` for all ports/services. But the `exitNodeACLs` allows them to use any device as an exit node, so they can route their internet traffic through the Tailscale network, but not access any internal services.
- **exitNodeACLs**: This is a [special feature](https://tailscale.com/kb/1104/exit-nodes/#restricting-who-can-use-exit-nodes) in Tailscale that allows you to restrict who can use which exit nodes.

### Notes

- If your servers are not tagged, you can use hostnames in the `"ports"` fields, e.g. `"server1:22"`.
- Remove or adjust the `"tagOwners"` section as needed to fit your tagging scheme.
- If you want to restrict servers group to TCP only (and not UDP), this ACL covers that, as Tailscale interprets `:22` as TCP by default.

