In PHP 8.2, there is no built-in coroutine or async/await support **in the core language**. However, you can achieve coroutine-like concurrency using libraries, such as:

- [`amphp/amp`](https://amphp.org/amp/)
- [`reactphp/event-loop`](https://reactphp.org/)

**amp** is one of the most popular libraries for this.

---

## Using `amphp/amp` to Limit Concurrent Coroutines

You can use [`Amp\Sync\LocalSemaphore`](https://amphp.org/amp/sync/semaphore/) to limit the number of concurrent coroutine (task) executions.

### Example: Maximum 5 Coroutines Running

First, install `amphp/amp` via Composer:

```sh
composer require amphp/amp
```

Then, use code like this:

```php
<?php

require 'vendor/autoload.php';

use Amp\Sync\LocalSemaphore;
use Amp\Sync\LocalKeyedMutex;
use Amp\Future;
use function Amp\async;
use function Amp\delay;

$semaphore = new LocalSemaphore(5); // Allow only 5 concurrent jobs

$jobs = [];
for ($i = 1; $i <= 20; $i++) {
    $jobs[] = async(function () use ($semaphore, $i) {
        $lock = $semaphore->acquire(); // Will wait if 5 coroutines already running
        try {
            echo "Starting job $i\n";
            yield delay(1000); // Simulate async work (1 second)
            echo "Finished job $i\n";
        } finally {
            $lock->release();
        }
    });
}

// Wait for all jobs to finish
Amp\Future\awaitAll($jobs);
```

**Output will show only 5 jobs starting at the same time.**

---

## Key Points

- Use a **semaphore** to limit concurrency.
- Use `async()` to launch coroutines.
- Always `release()` the semaphore lock after the job.

---

## Without Libraries: Not Possible

PHP's core doesn't support coroutines or async directly (yet). You **must** use an async/concurrency library like `amphp/amp` or `reactphp`.

---

## For ReactPHP

If you use [react/promise](https://github.com/reactphp/promise), you can limit concurrency using the [`react/promise`](https://github.com/reactphp/promise) `all()` pattern or by manually managing your queue.

---

## Summary

- Use `amphp/amp` for coroutines in PHP 8.2.
- Use `Amp\Sync\LocalSemaphore` to limit the number of concurrently running coroutines (jobs).
- Not possible with vanilla PHP alone.

