Certainly! Below is a Rust program that:

- Reads URLs from a file (one URL per line).
- Separates YouTube URLs from others.
- Downloads the YouTube URLs using [`yt-dlp`](https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp) via system calls.
- Prints non-YouTube URLs to the terminal.

### Assumptions

- The input file is named `urls.txt` (changeable in code).
- `yt-dlp` is installed and available in your `PATH`.

### Dependencies

Add this to your `Cargo.toml`:

```toml
[dependencies]
regex = "1"
```

---

### `main.rs`

```rust
use std::fs::File;
use std::io::{self, BufRead};
use std::process::Command;
use std::path::Path;
use regex::Regex;

fn main() -> io::Result<()> {
    // Change this if your input file has a different name
    let input_file = "urls.txt";

    // Compile regex for YouTube URLs
    let yt_regex = Regex::new(r"^(https?://)?(www\.)?(youtube\.com|youtu\.be)/").unwrap();

    // Open the file
    let file = File::open(input_file)?;
    let reader = io::BufReader::new(file);

    let mut youtube_urls = Vec::new();
    let mut other_urls = Vec::new();

    for line in reader.lines() {
        let url = line?.trim().to_string();
        if url.is_empty() { continue; }
        if yt_regex.is_match(&url) {
            youtube_urls.push(url);
        } else {
            other_urls.push(url);
        }
    }

    // Download YouTube URLs using yt-dlp
    for yt_url in youtube_urls {
        println!("Downloading: {}", yt_url);
        let status = Command::new("yt-dlp")
            .arg(&yt_url)
            .status();

        match status {
            Ok(s) if s.success() => println!("Downloaded: {}", yt_url),
            Ok(s) => eprintln!("yt-dlp failed with status: {}", s),
            Err(e) => eprintln!("Failed to run yt-dlp: {}", e),
        }
    }

    // Print other URLs
    if !other_urls.is_empty() {
        println!("\nNon-YouTube URLs found:");
        for url in other_urls {
            println!("{}", url);
        }
    }

    Ok(())
}
```

---

### Example `urls.txt`

```
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ
https://www.rust-lang.org/
https://youtu.be/ysz5S6PUM-U
https://example.com/
```

---

### How to Run

1. Add `regex` to your `Cargo.toml`.
2. Save the above code as `src/main.rs`.
3. Put your URLs in `urls.txt` in the project root.
4. Ensure `yt-dlp` is installed (`pip install yt-dlp` or from your package manager).
5. Run:

```sh
cargo run
```

